{% render 'section-style', section: section %}
{%- comment -%}
  NON Lotto — scratch and reveal.

  The design picked the prize in the browser from a weighted table and shipped
  the discount codes in the page source, which means anyone could read every
  code without scratching. Here the browser only draws the foil: the prize and
  its code come from the API, one draw per request, and the codes never exist
  in the document until the API has issued one.

  With no endpoint configured the widget stays closed — a scratch card with no
  prize behind it is worse than no scratch card.
{%- endcomment -%}

<div
  class="non-lotto"
  data-non-lotto
  data-endpoint="{{ settings.lotto_endpoint }}"
  data-reveal-path="{{ section.settings.reveal_path | default: '/lotto/reveal' }}"
  data-auto-open="{{ settings.lotto_auto_open | default: true }}"
  data-delay="{{ settings.lotto_delay | default: 1400 }}"
  data-cooldown-days="{{ settings.lotto_cooldown_days | default: 14 }}"
  data-reveal-at="{{ section.settings.reveal_at | default: 55 | divided_by: 100.0 }}"
  hidden>
  <div class="non-lotto__card" role="dialog" aria-modal="true" aria-labelledby="lotto-title">
    <div class="non-lotto__head">
      <span class="non-mono non-eyebrow">NON Lotto</span>
      <span class="non-lotto__ref" data-non-lotto-ref></span>
    </div>

    <div>
      <div class="non-lotto__title" id="lotto-title">{{ section.settings.heading }}</div>
      <p class="non-lotto__sub">{{ section.settings.subtext }}</p>
    </div>

    {%- comment -%}
      SCRATCH FIRST, EMAIL AFTER.

      This was the other way round: the email sat above the foil and nothing was
      scratchable until it had been submitted. Two problems, and the first one
      is fatal — the card LOOKS scratchable, so people scratch it, and nothing
      happens. There is no affordance saying "type here first"; there is a
      silver panel, which every human alive reads as scratch me.

      And it asked for the email before giving any reason to hand it over. Now
      the ritual comes first and the ask lands on a prize already won: scratch,
      see that something is yours, then claim it.

      Nothing is given away by re-ordering. The code never exists in the page
      until the API issues one — under the foil before claiming there is only
      the teaser below, which is copy, not a prize. The Worker remains the
      control; this is presentation.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- comment -%}
      A real close control, always present.

      Until now the only way out of this modal was the "No thanks" button in the
      footer, plus Escape. A phone has no Escape key, so on mobile that button
      was the single exit — and once someone has typed their email and claimed a
      prize, a button reading "No thanks" reads as giving the prize back. People
      correctly refuse to press it and end up trapped.

      Placed in the panel rather than floating over the scrim so it cannot land
      on top of the foil, and labelled for screen readers because a bare
      multiplication sign is not a word.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <button
      type="button"
      class="non-lotto__x"
      data-non-lotto-close
      aria-label="{{ 'general.accessibility.close' | t | default: 'Close' }}">&#215;</button>
    <div class="non-lotto__panel" data-non-lotto-panel>
      <div class="non-lotto__prize">
        {%- comment -%} What is under the foil before the claim. {%- endcomment -%}
        <div class="non-lotto__teaser" data-non-lotto-teaser>
          <div class="non-lotto__won">{{ section.settings.teaser_eyebrow }}</div>
          <div class="non-lotto__win">{{ section.settings.teaser_text }}</div>
        </div>

        {%- comment -%} And what replaces it once the API has issued a code. {%- endcomment -%}
        <div class="non-lotto__real" data-non-lotto-real hidden>
          <div class="non-lotto__won">{{ 'sections.lotto.won' | t }}</div>
          <div class="non-lotto__win" data-non-lotto-win></div>

          <button type="button" class="non-lotto__copy" data-non-lotto-copy hidden>
            <span class="non-lotto__copy-k" data-non-lotto-copy-label>{{ 'sections.lotto.code' | t }}</span>
            <b class="non-lotto__copy-v" data-non-lotto-code></b>
          </button>

          <div class="non-lotto__fine" data-non-lotto-terms></div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <canvas class="non-lotto__foil" data-non-lotto-foil aria-label="{{ section.settings.scratch_label | escape }}"></canvas>

      {%- comment -%}
        The blinking "SCRATCH HERE" nudge is gone. It was a mono line on the
        foil running a 2.4s blink, and a flashing label is the one thing on the
        page that never stops asking for attention.

        The instruction is not lost: the label still rides the canvas as its
        aria-label above, so it is announced to a screen reader, and the foil
        keeps cursor: pointer. The setting stays in the schema because that
        aria-label reads from it — deleting the setting would strip the
        accessible name too.
      {%- endcomment -%}
    </div>

    {%- comment -%}
      The claim. Hidden until the foil is off, then it is the only thing on the
      card asking for anything.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <form class="non-lotto__gate" data-non-lotto-gate hidden>
      <div class="non-lotto__claimhead">{{ section.settings.claim_heading }}</div>
      <div class="non-lotto__claim">
        <label class="visually-hidden" for="lotto-email">{{ 'sections.lotto.email_placeholder' | t }}</label>
        <input
          id="lotto-email"
          class="non-lotto__email"
          type="email"
          required
          autocomplete="email"
          inputmode="email"
          placeholder="{{ 'sections.lotto.email_placeholder' | t }}">
        <button type="submit" class="non-lotto__send" data-non-lotto-reveal>
          {{ section.settings.claim_label }}
        </button>
      </div>
    </form>
    <p class="non-error" data-non-lotto-error hidden></p>

    <p class="non-lotto__sent" data-non-lotto-sent hidden></p>

    <div class="non-lotto__foot">
      <span class="non-mono non-eyebrow" style="font-size:9.5px">
        {{ 'sections.lotto.while_stocks_last' | t }}
      </span>
      {%- comment -%}
        data-done-label is what this button becomes once a prize is claimed.
        Translated here rather than hardcoded in lotto.js, which has no access
        to the locale files.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <button
        type="button"
        class="non-lotto__no"
        data-non-lotto-close
        data-done-label="{{ 'sections.lotto.done' | t | default: 'Done' }}">
        {{ 'sections.lotto.no_thanks' | t }}
      </button>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<script src="{{ 'lotto.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "NON Lotto",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "heading",
      "label": "Heading",
      "default": "Scratch & reveal"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "scratch_label",
      "label": "Scratch prompt",
      "default": "Scratch here",
      "info": "Sits on the foil and fades on the first scratch."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "teaser_eyebrow",
      "label": "Under the foil — eyebrow",
      "default": "It's yours"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "teaser_text",
      "label": "Under the foil — line",
      "default": "One pour, with your name on it.",
      "info": "Shown after the scratch, before the email. No code exists at this point."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "claim_heading",
      "label": "Claim heading",
      "default": "Claim your prize"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "claim_label",
      "label": "Claim button",
      "default": "Claim it"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "reveal_path",
      "label": "Reveal path",
      "default": "/lotto/reveal",
      "info": "Appended to the endpoint in Theme settings."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "subtext",
      "label": "Subtext",
      "default": "Got to be in it, to win it. One gift per guest."
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "reveal_at",
      "label": "Reveal threshold",
      "min": 20,
      "max": 90,
      "step": 5,
      "unit": "%",
      "default": 55,
      "info": "How much foil has to be scratched away before the prize snaps open. Whole percentages only — Shopify validates ranges with (max - min) / step and decimal steps fail that check on floating point, which silently invalidates the whole section."
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Appearance"
    },
    {
      "type": "color",
      "id": "bg_color",
      "label": "Background"
    },
    {
      "type": "color",
      "id": "text_color",
      "label": "Text colour"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "font_family",
      "label": "Font",
      "options": [
        {
          "value": "",
          "label": "Theme default"
        },
        {
          "value": "sans",
          "label": "Helvetica (all text)"
        },
        {
          "value": "mono",
          "label": "JetBrains Mono (all text)"
        }
      ],
      "default": ""
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "text_scale",
      "label": "Text size",
      "min": 70,
      "max": 150,
      "step": 5,
      "unit": "%",
      "default": 100,
      "info": "Scales every text size in this section together."
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "section_padding",
      "label": "Vertical padding",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 160,
      "step": 8,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 0,
      "info": "0 keeps the section's own spacing."
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
